# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA) — required everywhere

Applies to site pages, edit mode, `/admin`, 404, every theme, and every new component. Gate: `npm run test:a11y` (`e2e/accessibility.spec.ts`, axe-core) + `src/lib/theme-contrast.test.ts`.

## Structure

- One `<h1>` per page (the page title). Content headings are h2–h4 and never skip a level.
- Landmarks: one `header` (banner), one `main#main-content`, one `footer` (contentinfo, owned by `PageShell`). Never nest `footer`/`header` landmarks; all content sits inside a landmark.
- Portals (dropdowns, settings) go to `portalRoot()` (inside `<main>`), never `document.body`.
- `html[lang]` and a non-empty `<title>` on every route.

## Keyboard & focus

- Everything works with keyboard alone; Tab order follows visual order. First Tab = "Skip to content".
- Never remove focus indicators. The global `:focus-visible` ring wins over `outline-none`; don't override it.
- Focus must not be hidden by the sticky header / editor bar (`scroll-padding` handles it — keep it the same in view and edit).
- Hover/focus popovers (`.edit-popover`): use `useEditPopover` — Escape dismisses, focus returns to the chip, `aria-expanded` is accurate.
- Portalled dropdowns: use `useDropdownA11y` — focus moves into the panel, Escape / Tab-out / outside click closes, focus returns to the trigger.

## Names, roles, states

- Every control has an accessible name; visible text must be part of it (`aria-label="Save changes"` for "Save").
- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label` + `aria-hidden` on the glyph. Toggles expose `aria-expanded`. Don't use `aria-haspopup` for disclosures.
- Status messages go to an always-mounted `role="status"` region (mounting it with the message is not announced).
- Images need `alt` (empty only if decorative). Inputs need a `<label>` or `aria-label`.

## Color & contrast

- Text ≥ 4.5:1 (large ≥ 3:1); UI component edges (inputs, selects) ≥ 3:1 → `--control-border`.
- Never fade a solid control with `opacity` at rest (it silently drops contrast).
- Dark sections remap tokens (`--inverse-*`); don't put `--foreground`/`--muted` text on a dark fill.
- Color is never the only signal (add text or a symbol: "✓ Saved!").
- New/changed theme tokens must pass `theme-contrast.test.ts`.

## Adaptable

- Reflow at 320px without horizontal scroll; survive WCAG text-spacing overrides.
- Targets ≥ 24×24px (edit chips are `--space-5`).
- Honour `prefers-reduced-motion` (global rule in `globals.css`).

## When you change UI

1. Check view **and** edit mode, in all 6 themes.
2. Add/extend a case in `e2e/accessibility.spec.ts` for new overlays, pages or interactive patterns.
3. Run `npm run test:a11y` when the user asks for verification.
